<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria sells 859 mln levs 6-mth coupon T-bills.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria sells 859 mln levs 6-mth coupon T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry on Wednesday sold 859 million levs of six-month floater coupon T-bills, yielding 117.70 percent to maturity, the central bank said.</p>
<p>The issue was offered with no par value or minimum acceptable price set in advance by the ministry.</p>
<p>The coupon equals the central bank's main interest rate, now set at 18 percent monthly or 216 percent annually.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow. The price is in percent of par:</p>
<p> Issue number		  BG3023997029</p>
<p> Type			    floater coupon</p>
<p> Term			    six months</p>
<p> Auction date		  April 2</p>
<p> Issue date		    April 2</p>
<p> Maturity date		 October 1</p>
<p> Bids received		 859 million levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids	   95.41</p>
<p> Bids approved		 859 million levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	  95.41 pct</p>
<p> Avg yield to maturity     117.70 pct</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
</text>
